From 9c84a2607c32cf03a84ace9f195450f3577c699f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bowen Wang <wangbowen1001@yahoo.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 00:47:51 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(scheduler): add a per-request waiting timeout

A request may carry waiting_timeout (seconds). When it has sat in the
scheduler's waiting queue longer than that, the existing timeout scan
aborts it with the response SGLANG_REQ_WAITING_TIMEOUT already produces.
The smaller of the two bounds applies, so a request can shorten the
operator's bound but not extend it. Accepted on /generate,
/v1/completions and /v1/chat/completions.

A server that never receives the field keeps today's scan: the queue is
walked only when the global bound is set or a request has carried one.
