From 6baf9e5d7e1ebddbd991d303895aa5877c3db7b8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bowen Wang <wangbowen1001@yahoo.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 02:01:56 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] perf(scheduler): test the two waiting bounds separately
 in the timeout scan

A queued request is dropped once it has outstayed either the global bound
or its own, which is the same rule as taking the smaller of the two without
the special case for a global value that is off. The request's bound is read
only on servers that have seen the field, so a server that uses only
SGLANG_REQ_WAITING_TIMEOUT pays one local check per queued request.
---
 python/sglang/srt/managers/scheduler.py | 19 +++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/python/sglang/srt/managers/scheduler.py b/python/sglang/srt/managers/scheduler.py
index 7bb7f0ba69..46a024cf91 100644
--- a/python/sglang/srt/managers/scheduler.py
+++ b/python/sglang/srt/managers/scheduler.py
